      "body": "# [H-02] UniswapPriceOracle TWAP Calculation Is a Mathematical Identity, Rendering Validation Useless and Exposing BuyBackBurner V2 Buybacks to Sandwich Attacks\n\n## Severity\n**High**\n\n## Vulnerability Type\nLoss of Funds\n\n## Affected Contracts\n- `contracts/oracles/UniswapPriceOracle.sol` — Broken TWAP calculation\n- `contracts/utils/BuyBackBurnerUniswap.sol` — V2 swap with `amountOutMin = 0`\n- `contracts/utils/BuyBackBurner.sol` — Relies on the broken oracle for slippage protection\n\n## Description\n\nThe TWAP (Time-Weighted Average Price) calculation in `UniswapPriceOracle.validatePrice()` contains a mathematical identity error: the computed `timeWeightedAverage` is **mathematically always equal to** the current spot price `tradePrice`, causing the function to **always return true** (except when `block.timestamp == blockTimestampLast`).\n\nAdditionally, `BuyBackBurnerUniswap._performSwap()` sets `amountOutMin = 0` for the V2 DEX swap, providing zero minimum output protection.\n\nThe combination of these two issues fully exposes the BuyBackBurner's V2 buyback operations to sandwich attacks, allowing attackers to extract value from the protocol's OLAS buyback-and-burn mechanism.\n\n## Vulnerable Code\n\n**Core Math Error — UniswapPriceOracle.sol lines 55-91:**\n\n```solidity\nfunction validatePrice(uint256 slippage) external view returns (bool) {\n    require(slippage <= maxSlippage, \"Slippage overflow\");\n\n    uint256 cumulativePriceLast;\n    if (direction == 0) {\n        cumulativePriceLast = IUniswapV2(pair).price1CumulativeLast();\n    } else {\n        cumulativePriceLast = IUniswapV2(pair).price0CumulativeLast();\n    }\n\n    (, , uint256 blockTimestampLast) = IUniswapV2(pair).getReserves();\n\n    if (block.timestamp == blockTimestampLast) {\n        return false;\n    }\n    uint256 elapsedTime = block.timestamp - blockTimestampLast;\n\n    uint256 tradePrice = getPrice();  // current spot price\n\n    // BUG: mathematical ident